# Client UI components (required)

Read `AGENTS.md` for full instructions.

## Arrow functions

Use arrow functions for components and helpers — `export const MyPage = () => { … }`, not `export function MyPage()`. See `AGENTS.md` → Code style.

## Reuse before creating

Search existing components first (`client/src/components/ui/` and related folders). Reuse `Button`, `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `Select`, `Textarea`, `FormField`, `FormActions`, `Modal`, `FormModal`, `Table`, `Tabs`, `PageContainer`, `PageHeader`, `Dropdown`, and `Spinner`. Create a new file only when no existing component fits.

**New** files: primitives → `components/ui/primitives/`; form composites → `components/ui/forms/`; navigation → `components/ui/navigation/`; layout → `components/layout/`; route guards → `routes/`. Do not move existing files. Do not duplicate a component that already exists in `components/ui/`.

## Page file organization

Keep page entry files thin. Do not migrate existing `pages/` files unless asked.

### Folder naming

- **Folders:** lowercase; **kebab-case** for multiple words (`super-admin`, `country-codes`, `audit-log`)
- **Files:** PascalCase page/components (`EmployeesPage.tsx`, `SiteSettingsPage.tsx`)
- Do not use camelCase, PascalCase, or snake_case for page folders

### Where pages go

| Audience | Folder | Examples |
|----------|--------|----------|
| **Super admin** | `client/src/pages/super-admin/<feature>/` | `dashboard/`, `companies/`, `site/`, `country-codes/` |
| **Tenant users** | `client/src/pages/<feature>/` or `pages/settings/<feature>/` | `employees/`, `settings/company/` |
| **New features** (greenfield) | `client/src/features/<feature>/` | same split: route entry, `components/`, optional `utils.ts` |

Add super-admin screens only under `pages/super-admin/`. Do not put them in `pages/settings/`.

Each feature: `<Feature>Page.tsx` + `components/` + optional `utils.ts` (path constants, formatters).

**Route-based tabs:** separate URLs per section → `NavTabBar` with `to` links (`super-admin/site/components/SiteSettingsTabs.tsx`). Use `PageContainer flushTop` when the tab bar bleeds under the header.

See `employees/EmployeesPage` and `super-admin/companies/RegistrationsPage` for page layout reference.

## Page layout

New dashboard pages must match existing screens (`employees/EmployeesPage`, `super-admin/companies/RegistrationsPage`):

- `PageContainer` → `PageHeader` (label, title, description, action button) → content
- Data lists: `Table` with `loading` / `emptyMessage` (center-aligned by default; use `align` prop to override)
- Create/edit: `FormModal` + `FormField`
- Related list views: `Tabs` with a separate `Table` per tab

## Table alignment

- Default: **center** for headers and cells
- Table-level: `<Table align="left" … />` sets default for all columns
- Column-level: `{ align: 'right' }` on a column overrides the table default
- Flex content in cells: use matching `justify-center` / `justify-start` / `justify-end` on inner flex wrappers

## Loading states

- `Button`: always pass `loading` + `loadingText` during async actions
- `Table`: use `loading` prop for list fetch states
- Never show a clickable submit button without a spinner while saving

## Save button activation

| Form type | Submit enabled when |
|-----------|---------------------|
| **Create** | All required fields filled (`areRequiredFieldsFilled`) |
| **Edit** | At least one field changed vs original (`hasFormChanges`) |

Use `submitDisabled` on `FormActions` / `FormModal`, or `disabled` on `Button`.

Helpers live in `client/src/utils/form.ts`: `areRequiredFieldsFilled`, `hasFormChanges`, `pickChangedFields`.

## Partial updates (DB)

- **Client:** PATCH/send only changed fields via `pickChangedFields`
- **Server:** Apply only fields present in the request body

## Password inputs

Use `PasswordInput` (show/hide toggle). Do not use raw `Input type="password"`.

## Icons

Use `react-icons/hi2` with colorful Tailwind classes on buttons, dropdown items, and actions.

## Form field icons (required)

**Every form control must have an icon** — all existing and new forms. Pass `icon` to every `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `Select`, and `Textarea` (`h-4 w-4 text-brand-600`). Do not use raw HTML form elements in forms.

- Company → `HiBuildingOffice2`
- Name → `HiUser`
- Email → `HiEnvelope`
- Password → `HiLockClosed`
- Search → `HiMagnifyingGlass`
- Phone → `HiPhone`
- Job title → `HiBriefcase`
- Department → `HiRectangleGroup`
- Date → `HiCalendarDays`
- Manager / team → `HiUserGroup`
- Status → `HiSignal`
- Notes / reason → `HiChatBubbleLeftEllipsis`

See `login/LoginForm`, `register/RegisterForm`, and `employees/CreateEmployeeModal` for reference.
